TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2): Space Mission Design","overview":"Develop a preliminary space-mission design that benefits Australia and report the mission concept and its space-segment elements. Use mission-design software of your choice, supported by hand calculations if useful, and justify the proposed design."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale. Include the following required information: What is the spacecraft's primary mission? Why is the mission needed? How many spacecraft are used and why? Who are the users (operator and customers)?","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all requirements to a high standard. Detailed descriptions and discussions are included. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions may feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements are not addressed. Poor descriptions or lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design. Present a summary of the mission design using software and/or hand calculations as appropriate. Include relevant screenshots and software files in the main body of the report and/or appendix. Include the following information: Where will it launch from, and using which launch vehicle? Why did you choose this option? What type of orbit will you use? What are its characteristics and orbital elements? Will you need to perform any orbital maneuvers? Which ground control facilities will you use? How often will your spacecraft be able to communicate with ground control? How long will the mission last, and what are your plans for EOL?","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high level understanding of the design procedure. Design clearly addresses mission and course concepts. Major requirements are all addressed and are well supported with quality evidence (e.g. software screenshots, software files, hand calculations, references from literature). Content is comprehensive, accurate, and persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding of the design procedure. Design may be inconsistent with regards to purpose and clarity of thought or feature errors. Major requirements are addressed but may lack some detail or are not well supported with evidence. Content may not be comprehensive and/or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding of the design procedure. Major requirements are not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content is incomplete or not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions reached from the evidence provided in the report."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions are reached but they may be generic or lack specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical engineering report structure. The report is easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Executive summary (or abstract) provides a concise overview of the report. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R4","met":"partial","where":"Mission Design / Launch"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R7","met":"partial","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R8","met":"partial","where":"Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R10","met":"partial","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R11","met":"no","where":"Bibliography"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Design / Launch","issue":"Kourou latitude stated as 45.05°N; actual is about 5.2°N, and the equatorial argument is therefore inconsistent."},{"where":"Mission Design / Launch","issue":"Vega E is not yet built and is selected as the baseline, while the text alternates between Vega C, Vega E and rideshare options without a clear decision."},{"where":"Orbit","issue":"Describes the orbit as retrograde and near-polar yet states it passes over almost the entire Earth; the 'constant sun angle' and J2 explanation conflate the RAAN drift sign and rate."},{"where":"Orbit","issue":"The 'Argument of Latitude' is stated as 0° while RAAN is said to change daily; the 'initial' epoch and RAAN source are not derived."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Access table repeats satellite number 13 and claims mean duration near 20 minutes; the summary table is inconsistent with the listed durations and the claim of constant contact is not supported."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"A 600 km circular orbit decays within years without propulsion; 5-year life is asserted without drag or lifetime analysis, and the drag sail discussion is incomplete."}],"overall":"The report covers all major mission segments with STK screenshots and a clear structure, but several technical errors (launch latitude, retrograde/SSO inconsistency, unsupported lifetime and contact claims), an unresolved launch vehicle choice, missing user identification, incomplete sentences, and Wikipedia citation weaken it substantially.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":5.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Mission purpose, rationale and single-spacecraft choice are addressed with reasonable justification and references. However, users (operator and customers) are not clearly identified, and the operator/customer discussion is missing. Some claims lack citation quality (Wikipedia used as source [6]), limiting the referencing standard.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Thus, only one satellite is required. This also just allows for simplicity in communications, reduces cost, and requires less time to build and launch."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Hundreds of millions of humans rely on reefs for food, natural protection, jobs, and tourism."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":30.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"Covers launch, orbit with Keplerian elements, ground station and access data, and EOL with screenshots. But launch site latitude is wrong (45.05°N for Kourou, which is ~5°N), the Vega E is not yet built and the launch is contradictory, RAAN 27.33° is not justified, the 'retrograde' claim conflicts with 87.8° SSO, the access table has duplicated numbering, no STK files are referenced, and EOL/manoeuvre analysis is thin and partly incoherent.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Design / Launch","quote":"The proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle"},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"the satellite will be positioned at an altitude of 600km above Earth’s surface"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"Systems Tool Kit 11 (STK) was used to calculate access periods as seen below:"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusion summarises segments and notes launch-date risk, but conclusions are generic and do not critically evaluate the evidence; claim of constant long-duration contact conflicts with the reported access data (gaps between passes).","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"The Mt Pleasant Radio Observatory is well-located to receive data from this orbit type constantly and for long durations."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear headings and numbered figures, but there are truncated sentences, a broken EOL paragraph, unlabeled/inconsistent tables, duplicated table numbering, Wikipedia cited despite prohibition, and a contents page referencing the wrong structure. Reference style is inconsistent and several sources are generic web URLs.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"Thus, abandoning the satellite at its EOL is not environmentally or socially responsible."},{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"The most promising alternative is a ‘drag sail’ – a drag-enhancing deorbit device that deploys at the EOL. It acts like a regular sail, utilising a large surface area to ‘ and is suitable"},{"where":"Contents","quote":"Executive Summary ..... 2"}]}]}
